# Python bytecode.
#
# ⚠️ These were TRACKED until 2026-09-01 — 40 .pyc files under dns_module/ and kv/, the two
# packages this repo ships. That is why `various updates` (fdb35f0) could be a commit
# containing nothing but bytecode: running the test suite dirtied the working tree and the
# artifacts were committed without anyone intending to.
#
# It matters more here than in an application repo, because this package ships BY TAG
# (`datazag-dns-module @ git+ssh://…@dns-module-v<N>`). A consumer installing a tag pulled
# whatever .pyc happened to be committed next to the source, with no guarantee the two
# agreed — stale bytecode beside fixed source is a silent way to ship the old behaviour.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class

# Test / tooling caches
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Packaging artefacts
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/

# Virtualenvs
.venv/
venv/

# ⚠️ DELIBERATELY NOT IGNORING `.env`. Two are tracked on purpose — `.env` and
# `dns_module/.env` — and they hold deployment TUNING, not secrets: nameserver lists, QPS and
# semaphore limits, timeouts, LMDB/lookup paths, feature flags, the Flight URL. Adding the
# usual `.env` rule here would not untrack them (ignore rules do not apply to tracked files),
# it would only make a future reader think they were protected when they are not. If a
# credential ever needs to live in this repo, that decision should be made deliberately and
# this comment revisited — not inherited from a boilerplate ignore file.
